+## Capability and release status
+
+The three status classes below are intentionally separate. A draft branch,
+green workflow, or design record is not a release or an activated service.
+
+| Surface | Status | Exact boundary |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| TypeScript package and `gkx` release line | Current release baseline | Version `2.1.2`; deterministic GKX processing, graph/export, proposal-only intelligence validation, and source-content-read-only Navigation. |
+| Functional uplift Phases 0-5 | Draft-qualified, unmerged | Full head `7b5262baee9fcda23d50b0cee0c4977d6e4305e7`; push run `32803396417`; PR run `32803399153`; draft PR #30. These coordinates qualify source and test evidence, not deployment or service activation. |
+| Functional uplift Phases 6-11 | Future planned work | Identity/MCP, graph projections and bounded tools, operator interfaces, packaging, final documentation, and integration remain unavailable until implemented and qualified in dependency order. |
+
+No Phase 6 work is released or operational. In particular, there is no
+qualified multi-agent identity system, MCP server, governed external-effects
+plane, activated Phase 5 watcher service, or Phase 7 graph-query service.
+Phase 5 contains draft contracts and reference/qualification behavior; it does
+not by itself enable a product service or authorize source mutation.
+
+### Authority allocation
+
+- `gkos-standard` owns normative GKOS/GKX meaning.
+- Full is the platform-neutral TypeScript contract and reference-behavior
+  authority for this uplift.
+- Lite may consume exact Full packs and implement private Rust conformance. It
+  must not become a second parser, identity system, lineage model, or semantic
+  authority.
+- Optional models, providers, graph systems, and transports are adapters. They
+  do not receive governance authority.
+
+### Sensitivity and access-control boundary
+
+`sensitivity` is projection metadata used by caller-supplied policy. Defaulting
+an absent or invalid value to `secret` is a conservative projection rule, not
+an authorization system. The current loopback APIs do not hide records merely
+because of their sensitivity label. A host must authenticate the caller,
+enforce its own authorization and discoverability policy before disclosure,
+and treat the projected sensitivity value as an additional policy input.
+
+### Required defect gate before Phase 6
+
+At base head `7b5262b`, `bin/gkx.mjs` can read `uid` or `sensitivity` text from
+outside a delimited frontmatter block on the CLI `nav context` path. The
+library API remains usable with caller-built snapshots and a correctly
+enforced discoverability policy. A bounded, BOM-aware frontmatter repair and a
+fenced-YAML regression test exist on the uncommitted continuation branch, but
+were still pending the complete independent gate when this reconciliation was
+prepared. Therefore:
+
+- do not advertise or use CLI `nav context` as a security boundary at this
+  base coordinate;
+- complete the repair, independent review, focused regression, broad suite,
+  and hosted qualification before Phase 6; and
+- during Phase 10, replace this status with the exact qualified repair commit
+  and runs before applying this README patch.
+
+## Future planned sequence
+
+1. **Phase 6:** multi-agent identity, credential lifecycle, revocation, and
+   bounded MCP transport facades.
+2. **Phase 7:** disposable durable graph projections and policy-checked,
+   citation-bearing bounded graph tools.
+3. **Phase 8:** operator interfaces that expose only qualified APIs and keep
+   reads, proposals, approvals, and committed effects distinct.
+4. **Phase 9:** clean-machine Full distribution and separately governed Lite
+   packaging with linkage, CPU/OS, checksum, SBOM, and license evidence.
+5. **Phase 10:** documentation reconciliation against terminal behavior and
+   artifacts, including this successor patch.
+6. **Phase 11:** exact Full/Lite pin reconciliation, end-to-end qualification,
+   and owner handoff.
+
+None of those plans authorizes merge, tag, release, publication, deployment,
+service activation, or external effects.
+
